---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Crumbs from '../components/Crumbs.astro';
import { countries } from '../data/countries';
import { DATA_CHECKED, globalSources } from '../data/sources';
import { formatDate } from '../lib/visa';
---
<Base title="How we check entry rules" description="Where Bemba's visa and health information comes from, how often it is checked, and how to report a change.">
  <div class="wrap narrow">
    <section class="page-head">
      <Crumbs items={[{ name: 'How we check', href: '/about/' }]} />
      <p class="eyebrow">Method</p>
      <h1 class="h1">How we check entry rules.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Bemba collects visa, vaccine and arrival rules for all 54 African countries in one place, with a link to the official source.</p>
    </section>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2 class="h2">Sources</h2>
      <p>Visa rules come from official government portals where they exist, the per-nationality visa requirement tables on Wikipedia (cross-checked between several EU, UK and US passports), and news reports of recent changes. Yellow fever rules come from the World Health Organization country list, with the US State Department country pages where they are stricter. Every country page lists the exact sources used.</p>
      <ul>{globalSources.map((s) => <li><a href={s.url} rel="noopener" target="_blank">{s.label}</a></li>)}</ul>
      <h2 class="h2">When it was checked</h2>
      <p>All {countries.length} countries were last checked on {formatDate(DATA_CHECKED)}. The date is shown on every page.</p>
      <h2 class="h2">Report a change</h2>
      <p>Rules change, sometimes overnight. If you notice something out of date, email <span class="mono">hello@bemba.com</span> with the country and a link to the source, and we will update the page.</p>
      <h2 class="h2">What Bemba is not</h2>
      <p>Bemba is a travel guide, not a visa agency, a lawyer or a doctor. We never charge for visas. Apply only on the official portal, and get medical advice from a travel clinic.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
